	(text "MAX-M10S, the only GNSS on the board (the Connect Kit nRF9151 GNSS is not used,\nso GNSS never has to share the LTE radio). RF straight from the bias tee on sheet 14;\nRF_IN is DC blocked inside the module, VCC_RF unused.\nGNSS_ENABLE -> PP3V3_GNSS: VCC/V_IO and the active antenna bias together.\nGNSS_BCKP_EN -> PP3V3_GNSS_BCKP (S7U1, sheet 7) -> V_BCKP. Firmware chooses:\n  both off: 0 uA, cold start (~29 s unassisted)\n  BCKP on, main off: HW backup mode, 32 uA typ, RTC + ephemeris kept for ~1 s hot starts\n  (ephemeris is good for ~4 h; past that it is a warm start). S1R3 holds BCKP off through reset.\nBefore dropping PP3V3_GNSS, drive the MCU TX low or float it: an idle-high TX\nback-feeds V_IO through S16R3 (1k series on both UART lines limits it).\nPP3V3_GNSS_ST for rail fault detection; TIMEPULSE gives a fix-valid / 1PPS edge.\nActive antenna gain >= 15 dB: set the internal LNA to bypass (CFG-HW-RF_LNA_MODE).\nSiP32431 140 us rise meets the VCC and V_BCKP ramp limit (>= 25 us/V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ebd4fd16-5980-4d27-82fe-0c3c4c4174c2")
	)
	(text "15"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 184.658 183.388 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ef4a40ac-a3e8-45dd-b836-4d13d905a87f")
	)
